## Clear boundaries (trust is part of the product)

Please read these as features of an honest sale, not as fine print to hide:

1. **Normal mode is one active chain.** Backups help with failover. Parallel multipath send is not the default story.
2. **Load-aware ranking only helps when load is actually reported into the peer table.** The mechanism exists; integration quality matters.
3. **Lab and emulation are evidence of engineering, not a field SLA.** Your topology decides the real numbers.
4. **Security building blocks ≠ full identity platform.** Transport protection and selected authentication options exist; PKI, policy, and key lifecycle are buyer-side work.
5. **Old marketing lines** (fixed “380 ms”, “75% less traffic”, “works at 25% loss” as universal facts) are **not** claims we stand behind in this package. Use pilot data.

