## How a deal usually moves

1. **Conversation** — is the problem real for you (multi-hop + degradation + costly resend/repair)?  
2. **Materials** — One-Pager, draft, architecture status.  
3. **NDA + package** (if full source is not public) — build, tests, code reading.  
4. **Pilot design** — one topology, few success metrics, explicit non-goals.  
5. **Decision** — walk away, OEM license, or **full technology transfer**.

If you only need a managed service with an operator SLA, this may not be the right shape of deal.  
If you want **to own a resilience layer inside your stack**, this is the shape we optimised for.

